+## Submission Envelope and Acceptance
+
 - [ ] **REC-001**: When an authenticated worker submits a valid visit edit, the system SHALL retain the submitted payload with its visit ID, author ID, and server receipt time.
 - [ ] **REC-002**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with an identical payload, the system SHALL return the original acceptance result without creating another stored submission.
 - [ ] **REC-003**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with a different payload, the system SHALL reject the submission and leave the original submission unchanged.
-- [ ] **REC-004**: When edits derived from the same starting visit state are accepted, the system SHALL preserve both original submissions regardless of the concurrency policy's outcome.
-- [ ] **REC-005**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL indicate whether unresolved review work exists for that visit.
-- [ ] **REC-006**: When a coordinator resolves review work, the system SHALL retain the coordinator's identity and the contributing submission IDs with the resolution outcome.
+- [ ] **REC-004**: When a worker submits a valid visit edit, the system SHALL validate that the submission includes a base revision ID, a complete visit record, an idempotency key, and the worker's authenticated identity.
+
+## Revision Creation and Assignment
+
+- [ ] **REC-010**: When an authenticated submission is accepted, the system SHALL assign a server-generated revision ID and store the complete submitted visit record under that revision.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: When a revision is created, the system SHALL record its base revision ID, the submitted visit record, the author ID, the server receipt timestamp, and the idempotency key.
+- [ ] **REC-012**: When a revision is created from a base revision, the system SHALL preserve that relationship so the revision chain is reconstructible.
+
+## Competing Revisions and Unresolved Work
+
+- [ ] **REC-020**: When a submission's base revision ID matches a revision that is not the current revision, the system SHALL determine whether competing revisions exist (one or more other revisions sharing the same base).
+- [ ] **REC-021**: When competing revisions are detected (multiple revisions with the same base revision ID), the system SHALL mark the visit as having unresolved review work and retain all competing revisions.
+- [ ] **REC-022**: When a submission's base revision ID matches the current revision, the system SHALL accept the submission without creating competing work.
+
+## Current Revision and Unresolved State
+
+- [ ] **REC-030**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL identify and return the current revision—the latest revision in the chain where no competing siblings exist.
+- [ ] **REC-031**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL indicate whether the visit has unresolved review work (competing revisions exist).
+- [ ] **REC-032**: When a visit has unresolved review work, the system SHALL return the identities and full records of all competing revisions alongside the current revision.
+- [ ] **REC-033**: The system SHALL treat a visit with a single revision or a resolved chain of non-competing revisions as having no unresolved review work.
+
+## Revision History Preservation
+
+- [ ] **REC-040**: The system SHALL preserve the complete chain of revisions for each visit, including abandoned competing branches, so revision history remains auditable.
+- [ ] **REC-041**: When a coordinator resolves review work, the system SHALL retain the originally submitted records of all competing revisions unchanged.
+
+## Resolution Operations
+
+- [ ] **REC-050**: When a coordinator selects a competing revision to resolve review work, the system SHALL record the resolution with the selected revision ID, competing revision IDs, coordinator identity, and resolution timestamp.
+- [ ] **REC-051**: After resolution, the system SHALL update the selected revision to become the current revision.
+- [ ] **REC-052**: When future submissions name a resolved revision (or its descendants) as their base, the system SHALL treat the submission as building on the accepted chain without creating competing work.
+- [ ] **REC-053**: When a submission names an abandoned competing revision as its base, the system SHALL create a new competing branch rooted at that abandoned revision.
+
+## Original Submission Preservation
+
+- [ ] **REC-060**: The system SHALL preserve each original submitted payload with metadata (visit ID, revision ID, author, receipt time, idempotency key) unchanged after acceptance, even if competing revisions are later resolved.
